ulus\n    while exponent > 0:\n        if exponent % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % modulus\n        exponent = exponent >> 1\n        base = (base * base) % modulus\n    return result\n\ndef count_permutations(n, stairs):\n    mod = 998244353\n    dp = [[0] * (n+1) for _ in range(n+1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n+1):\n        for j in range(n+1):\n            if dp[i][j] > 0:\n                for k in stairs:\n                    limit = min(j+k-1, n)\n                    if i+max(0, max(0, k-j-1)) < limit:\n                        dp[i+k][limit] = (dp[i+k][limit] + dp[i][j]) % mod\n    \n    return dp[n][n]\n```\nscore float 0.0\nstep int 200\nacc float 0.0\npass_rate float 0.0\n\nFILE validation_data/0.jsonl count 184 keys ['input', 'output', 'score', 'step', 'reward', 'acc', 'pass_rate', 'fail_debug']\ninput str system\nYou are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant.\nuser\nPlease write a python program to address the following QUESTION. Your ANSWER should be in a code block format like this: ```python # Write your code here ```. \nQUESTION:\nA $\\mathbf{0}$-indexed array $a$ of size $n$ is called good if for all valid indices $i$ ($0 \\le i \\le n-1$), $a_i + i$ is a perfect square$^\\dagger$.\n\nGiven an integer $n$. Find a permutation$^\\ddagger$ $p$ of $[0,1,2,\\ldots,n-1]$ that is good or determine that no such permutation exists.\n\n$^\\dagger$ An integer $x$ is said to be a perfect square if there exists an integer $y$ such that $x = y^2$.\n\n$^\\ddagger$ An array $b$ is a permutation of an array $a$ if $b$ consists of the elements of $a$ in arbitrary order. For example, $[4,2,3,4]$ is a permutation of $[3,2,4,4]$ while $[1,2,2]$ is not a permutation of $[1,2,3]$.\n\n\n-----Input-----\n\nThe first line contains a single integer $t$ ($1 \\le t \\le 10^4$) — the number of test cases.\n\nThe only line of each test case contains a single integer $n$ ($1 \\le n \\le 10^5$) — the length of the permutation 